      "content": "I am currently reviewing literature regarding the statistical challenges of genome-wide association studies (GWAS), specifically concerning the estimation of polygenic scores for complex phenotypic traits across diverse ancestral populations. \n\nCould you provide a technical overview of the methodologies used to differentiate between true causal variants and those that appear significant due to population stratification? I'm particularly interested in how researchers utilize principal component analysis (PCA) and linear mixed models (LMMs) to account for varying allele frequency distributions across different geographic clusters to ensure that observed phenotypic variance is not being confounded by ancestral background.",
